# Spec Memory

Every time you are asked to do something, you MUST check the specifications first.
You MUST rely ENTIRELY on the specifications to understand the project.
You MUST read ALL specification files.
You're ONLY allowed to avoid reading the spec if you're asked something quick and generic.

## Core Files

1. spec/projectbrief.md

   - Why this project exists
   - Problems it solves
   - How it should work
   - Defines core requirements and goals
   - What is in scope and what is out of scope

2. spec/progress.md

   - What's done
   - Current focus
   - Next steps
   - Learnings & insights

3. spec/systemPatterns.md

   - System architecture
   - Key technical decisions
   - Design patterns in use
   - Component relationships (using flowchart diagrams)
   - Critical implementation paths (with sequence diagrams if necessary)

4. spec/techContext.md

   - Main Language used in the project
   - Development & Production Runtimes
   - External Services
   - Technical constraints
   - Other tools used in the project

5. spec/domain.md

   - Describe Entities and their relationships in high level language
   - Use Cases

```mermaid
flowchart TD
   PB[projectbrief.md]
   D[domain.md]
   S[systemPatterns.md]
   T[techContext.md]
   PR[progress.md]
   PB --> D --> PR
   PB --> S --> PR
   PB --> T --> PR
```

